    <!-- MISSION SECTION -->
    <section id="mission" data-page="home">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="sec-head">
          <div class="label"><span class="zh">核心理念与使命</span><span class="en">Philosophy &amp; Mission</span><span class="ms">Falsafah &amp; Misi</span></div>
          <h2 class="display"><span class="zh">健美，不应该只是<span class="gold-text">健全人士</span>的舞台</span><span class="en">Bodybuilding is not only a stage for the <span class="gold-text">able-bodied</span></span><span class="ms">Bina badan bukan sekadar pentas untuk mereka yang <span class="gold-text">sempurna tubuh badan</span></span></h2>
          <p class="lead">
            <span class="zh">每个人都应该拥有展示自己、挑战自己及参与竞技体育的机会。对 OKU 运动员而言，参赛不只是为了奖牌，更是通过运动建立自信、突破自我，并向社会展示他们的能力与价值。</span>
            <span class="en">Everyone deserves the chance to show who they are, test themselves and compete. For OKU athletes, competing is about more than medals. It builds confidence, breaks personal limits and shows society what they are capable of.</span><span class="ms">Setiap orang berhak mendapat peluang untuk menunjukkan jati diri, menguji kemampuan diri dan bertanding. Bagi atlet OKU, bertanding bukan sekadar mengejar pingat. Ia membina keyakinan diri, mematahkan had peribadi dan menunjukkan kepada masyarakat apa yang mampu mereka lakukan.</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pillars">
          <article class="pillar">
            <h3><span class="zh">打破社会对残障人士的刻板印象</span><span class="en">Break the stereotypes about disability</span><span class="ms">Menepis tanggapan stereotaip tentang kecacatan</span></h3>
            <p><span class="zh">社会往往从身体的限制来看待 OKU 群体，却忽略了他们同样拥有梦想、目标及追求卓越的能力。</span><span class="en">Society often sees OKU through their physical limits, and overlooks that they have dreams, goals and the drive to excel.</span><span class="ms">Masyarakat sering menilai OKU berdasarkan had fizikal mereka, lalu terlepas pandang bahawa mereka juga mempunyai impian, matlamat dan semangat untuk cemerlang.</span></p>
            <p class="pull"><span class="zh">我们希望社会看到的，是他们为了实现目标所付出的努力。</span><span class="en">We want people to see the effort behind every goal they chase.</span><span class="ms">Kami mahu orang ramai melihat usaha di sebalik setiap matlamat yang mereka kejar.</span></p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar">
            <h3><span class="zh">建立自信，从参与者成为运动员</span><span class="en">Build confidence: from participant to athlete</span><span class="ms">Membina keyakinan diri: daripada peserta kepada atlet</span></h3>
            <p><span class="zh">身体的限制、社会眼光及缺乏机会，可能让一些 OKU 人士逐渐失去自信。站上比赛舞台，面对评委与观众，获得的不只是比赛经验，更是一份对自己的肯定。</span><span class="en">Physical limits, social attitudes and a lack of opportunity can wear down confidence. Standing in front of judges and an audience gives self-recognition.</span><span class="ms">Had fizikal, sikap masyarakat dan kekurangan peluang boleh menghakis keyakinan diri. Berdiri di hadapan juri dan penonton memberi pengiktirafan terhadap diri sendiri.</span></p>
            <p class="pull"><span class="zh">不只是需要帮助的人，也是有梦想、有目标、有能力的运动员。</span><span class="en">Not only a person who needs help, but an athlete with dreams, goals and ability.</span><span class="ms">Bukan sekadar insan yang memerlukan bantuan, tetapi atlet yang mempunyai impian, matlamat dan keupayaan.</span></p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar">
            <h3><span class="zh">创造公平及包容的竞技机会</span><span class="en">Create fair and inclusive competition</span><span class="ms">Mewujudkan pertandingan yang adil dan inklusif</span></h3>
            <p><span class="zh">OKU 运动员在身体条件、肌肉控制、活动能力及训练方式上可能与一般运动员不同。我们推动更具包容性的 Adaptive Bodybuilding，并关注赛事资讯与合作资源。</span><span class="en">OKU athletes may differ in physical condition, muscle control and training. We push for more inclusive Adaptive Bodybuilding and partnerships.</span><span class="ms">Atlet OKU mungkin berbeza dari segi keadaan fizikal, kawalan otot dan latihan. Kami memperjuangkan Adaptive Bodybuilding yang lebih inklusif serta kerjasama yang lebih luas.</span></p>
            <p class="pull"><span class="zh">让不同身体能力的人，都能在适合自己的环境中发挥潜能。</span><span class="en">So every body can compete in an environment that suits it.</span><span class="ms">Supaya setiap tubuh dapat bertanding dalam persekitaran yang sesuai dengannya.</span></p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar">
            <h3><span class="zh">培育马来西亚 Adaptive Bodybuilding 人才</span><span class="en">Develop Malaysian Adaptive Bodybuilding talent</span><span class="ms">Membangunkan bakat Adaptive Bodybuilding Malaysia</span></h3>
            <p><span class="zh">我们希望发掘更多有潜力的 OKU 健美运动员，鼓励他们参与本地及国际自然健美赛事，并与体育组织、赛事单位、教练及企业建立合作。</span><span class="en">We want to find more promising OKU bodybuilders and encourage them to enter local and international natural bodybuilding events.</span><span class="ms">Kami ingin mencari lebih ramai pembina badan OKU yang berpotensi dan menggalakkan mereka menyertai pertandingan bina badan semula jadi di peringkat tempatan dan antarabangsa.</span></p>
            <p class="pull"><span class="zh">让本地运动员未来有机会站上国际舞台。</span><span class="en">So Malaysian athletes can one day stand on the international stage.</span><span class="ms">Supaya atlet Malaysia suatu hari nanti dapat berdiri di pentas antarabangsa.</span></p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="mission-end">
          <p class="display" style="max-width:none"><span class="zh">最终目标：让 OKU 不只是观看比赛的人，也能够成为<span class="gold-text">站在舞台上的运动员</span>。</span><span class="en">Our end goal: OKU are not only people who watch the competition. They compete in it.</span><span class="ms">Matlamat akhir kami: OKU bukan sekadar penonton pertandingan. Mereka turut bertanding.</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

